# Alienorum exoplanet host astrometry supplement v5; audited 2026-10-16.
# 52 accepted hosts: 49 pass the initial astrometric screen; three have elevated RUWE.
# ICRS Gaia DR3 positions propagated from epoch 2016.0 to 2000.0 with
# Gaia pmra (includes cos(dec)) and pmdec; first-order angular propagation.
# Distance: Bailer-Jones et al. (2021) geometric posterior median, 16/84 percentiles.
# Catalog measurements can still disagree with older stellar parameters.
# Identity: SIMBAD identifier joins, published SOI identifiers, expanded SDSS identity.
# Sources: https://simbad.cds.unistra.fr/simbad/sim-tap
# https://dc.zah.uni-heidelberg.de/tableinfo/gaia.dr3lite
# https://dc.zah.uni-heidelberg.de/tableinfo/gedr3dist.main
# https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.05220
# https://arxiv.org/html/2304.01076v1 (SOI-4 and SOI-8)
# 2MASS J18452562+4339300 uses KOI-6925 A, Gaia DR3 2117261032589510272.
# Component A assignment accepted from position, luminosity, and color consistency.
# KIC 6372194: precise SIMBAD position and brightness/color agreement.
# LPI-7913 is KOI-6532; position and brightness/color agreement.
# https://www.exoplanet.eu/catalog/koi_6532_b--6213/
# EX Dra (AB): RUWE 1.714; strong parallax, accreting binary; accepted with caveat.
# KIC 10255705: RUWE 1.835; color agreement and excess brightness; accepted with caveat.
# Distance intervals are formal posterior quantiles, not bounds on binary systematics.
# KOI-5: RUWE 4.891; accepted as a host without the rejected EU planet.
# KOI-5: NASA V=11.713, 5766 K, radius 1.73 solar; SIMBAD spectral type G2V.
# https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/overview/KOI-5
# Optional columns after Gaia ID: V|spectral_type|teff_K|radius_solar
# Fallback only: preserve complete upstream positions and distances.
